<Base title="Finances" description="Alabama Section funds: what comes in, what it may be spent on, and the annual accounting to member clubs.">
  <PageHead title="Finances" lede="The Section runs on a small annual fee from each member club. USPSA policy requires a full accounting to the clubs every year; this page is where it gets published." />
  <div class="container">
    <GovNav />

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Income</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Club fee:</strong> $20 per member club per year, due before 30 January (Bylaws Art. 7.E).</li>
        <li><strong>Per-shooter activity fee:</strong> USPSA allows a Section to levy up to $1.00 per contestant per sanctioned match if its bylaws provide for it (Policy §5.1). The Alabama bylaws currently do not; the Section relies on the flat club fee.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Allowable expenses</h2>
      <p>Costs of the Section Coordinator's office and projects that benefit all Section clubs: the website and domain, postage, printing, phone. Not allowed: travel, meals, lodging, or match entry fees for club, Section, Area, or National matches (Art. 7.E; Policy §5.2).</p>

      <h2>Annual accounting</h2>
      <p>Rendered to the clubs at the annual meeting and posted here (Policy §5.3). Funds transfer to a new Section Coordinator by 15 January of their term.</p>

      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Opening balance</th><th>Income</th><th>Expenses</th><th>Closing balance</th><th>Statement</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>2026</td><td colspan="5"><span class="soon">Coming soon</span></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
